OL,3,AHarper Lee first edition novel found in
OL,4,AOxfam shop
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rare first edition of the novel To
OL,7,FKill A Mockingbird has been found among
OL,8,Fitems donated to Oxfam, according to
OL,9,Fthe charity.
OL,11,FThe copy of Harper Lee's seminal 1960
OL,12,Fwork was discovered in a box of
OL,13,FAmerican books given to the charity's
OL,14,Fbookshop in Portobello Road, west
OL,15,FLondon.
OL,17,FIt has since been acquired by the
OL,18,FBritish Library and will join its
OL,19,Fnational collection.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,164,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11915
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790093893
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AHarper Lee first edition novel found in
OL,4,AOxfam shop
OL,5,
OL,6,FShop manager Olivia Haysman-Walker, who
OL,7,Fidentified the copy as being a first US
OL,8,Fedition, said the book could easily
OL,9,Fhave been missed. "There were lots of
OL,10,Fbooks to work through in the donation,
OL,11,Fbut we recognised To Kill A Mockingbird
OL,12,Fand thought it was worth taking a
OL,13,Fcloser look."
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG15/19
